---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import tutors from '../../data/tutors.json';
---
<Base title="A-level English tutors: English Language and Literature, online one-to-one" description="Online one-to-one A-level English Language and English Literature tutoring for AQA and the other boards, from experienced A-level English teachers. Paid trial lesson, no packages." context="tutors" leadLine="Tell us the year group, the subject and exam board, the target grade and your availability, and we will arrange a trial lesson.">
  <h1>Your A-level English tutor</h1>
  <p>Online one-to-one lessons for AS and A-level English Language and English Literature with experienced A-level English teachers who know what the examiners reward: close analysis with precise terminology, context used to explain meaning rather than bolted on, other readings weighed rather than listed, and an argument that holds together from the first line to the conclusion.</p>
  {tutors.map((tutor) => <section class="tutor">
    <div class="tutor-head">
      {tutor.photo ? <img class="tutor-photo" src={tutor.photo} alt={tutor.name} width="160" height="160" /> : <div class="tutor-photo tutor-initial" aria-hidden="true">{tutor.name[0]}</div>}
      <div><h2>{tutor.name}</h2><p class="muted">{tutor.title}</p></div>
    </div>
    {tutor.bio.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
    <ul>{tutor.offers.map((o) => <li>{o}</li>)}</ul>
  </section>)}
  <section class="tutor"><h2>What lessons cover</h2><ul><li>English Language: text analysis across the language levels, child language acquisition, language diversity and change, discourses, the opinion article and the NEA (Language in Action)</li><li>English Literature: your Shakespeare play and set texts, the love poetry anthology, unseen poetry and prose, the WW1 or Modern times paper and the NEA (Independent critical study)</li><li>Essay planning and timed writing, with answers marked against AQA's levels and bands</li><li>Other boards too: Edexcel, OCR and Eduqas English Language and English Literature</li></ul></section>
  <h2>Fees and how it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>{tutors.length && tutors.every((t) => t.fee) ? tutors[0].fee : 'Fee on enquiry'}</strong>, online, one-to-one. The first lesson is a paid trial; if it isn't right for you there is no obligation to continue.</li>
    <li>No packages and nothing to buy in advance: you pay lesson by lesson.</li>
    <li>Most students have one or two lessons a week at a regular slot, which is what moves a grade.</li>
  </ul>
  <ol>
    <li>Message us on WhatsApp or send the enquiry form with the year, the subject and exam board, the target grade and the times that work for you.</li>
    <li>We match you with the tutor who fits best, and they get in touch to arrange the trial lesson.</li>
    <li>Lessons are booked directly with your tutor from then on.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="muted">DBS-checked; references available. AQA past papers by subject: <a href="/language/">English Language</a> · <a href="/literature/">English Literature A</a>.</p>
</Base>
